    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it's green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the salutation rule (`salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given) with minimal structural impact.\n\n**Changes (4 files, all small/cohesive):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an input `title` field to `OwnerFields` and a read-only `salutation` field to `Owner`. These regenerate into the DTOs so Jackson binds `title` on POST and serializes `salutation` on GET.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with a plain getter/setter, plus a self-contained `getSalutation()` (CC 2):\n   ```java\n   public String getSalutation() {\n       return (this.title == null || this.title.isBlank()) ? this.lastName : this.title + \" \" + this.lastName;\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title VARCHAR(10)` column to the `owners` table (tests run under the hsqldb profile with `ddl-auto=none`).\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended the trailing `NULL` to each seed `owners` row so the positional inserts still match the new column count.\n\n**Why this keeps structural cost low:** the derivation relies entirely on MapStruct's automatic property-name matching (`OwnerFieldsDto.title \u2192 Owner.title`, `Owner.getSalutation() \u2192 OwnerDto.salutation`), so the large `OwnerMapper` interface was left untouched \u2014 no `@AfterMapping` method added to a high-WMC class. The only Java change is three trivial, low-complexity methods on `Owner`; the rest are declarative schema/data edits with no functions.",
